User Experience Flow
When users open the website, they see a welcome screen titled **“TechWords Fun – Learn Tech the Easy Way.”** Soft and pleasant background music begins playing to create a relaxing learning environment.

As users scroll down the page, each technology term appears individually with smooth animations such as fade-in, slide-in, or pop-up transitions. Showing one word at a time keeps the experience focused and engaging.

Interactive Features
The website should include a **“Teach Me a Random Tech Word”** button that displays a random technology term and its explanation. This adds an element of surprise and encourages users to explore more words.

Categories may also be included so users can explore groups such as AI terms, programming terms, networking terms, and internet terminology.

Visual Design
The design should include bright colors, smooth gradients, and modern typography. Small illustrations or emojis can accompany each term to make the interface friendly and easy to understand.

Audio Experience
Soft and cheerful background music should play while users explore the website. Optional sound effects can play whenever a new word appears to enhance the interactive feeling.

Goal
The main goal of the website is to transform learning technology vocabulary into a fun and interactive experience that feels like browsing an entertaining educational reel instead of reading a traditional glossary page.
